{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted","id":364042,"title":"Reckoning Vs Hunted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-08T20:01:36-08:00","id":364042,"title":"Reckoning Vs Hunted","content":"Thoughts on the Imbued from Hunter the Reckoning, vs Hunters who are just mortals with a vendetta, or members of the government, church or some such.<br /> <br /> Which do you prefer?<br /> <br /> Reckoning seems to have largely displaced the more traditional hunters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T20:20:35-08:00","id":364054,"title":"","content":"I preffer Reckoning, its more epic in scope","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T21:03:44-08:00","id":364087,"title":"","content":"I'd wish Reckoning and everything associated with it would burn in eternal hell-fire and never be heard from again.<br /> <br /> So the answer is I'd prefer the Hunters that are presented in Hunters Hunted and other year of the hunter products. After all the imbued are not &quot;hunters&quot; they are just slightly weaker bunch of supernatural creatures who are manipulated by stronger bunch of supernatural creatures, that book if anything was about false advertising and remains only WoD line that I have sold all the books away from, and not because of monetary gain but just to get rid of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T21:32:19-08:00","id":364090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364087#post364087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wish Reckoning and everything associated with it would burn in eternal hell-fire and never be heard from again.<br /> <br /> So the answer is I'd prefer the Hunters that are presented in Hunters Hunted and other year of the hunter products. After all the imbued are not &quot;hunters&quot; they are just slightly weaker bunch of supernatural creatures who are manipulated by stronger bunch of supernatural creatures, that book if anything was about false advertising and remains only WoD line that I have sold all the books away from, and not because of monetary gain but just to get rid of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>hey posessed, whats with the hatred for hunter, i never understand it but perhaps you could enlight me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T22:08:39-08:00","id":364120,"title":"","content":"It's a personal dislike and probably somewhat of a grudge gotten from the fact that when the game came out it advertised itself as humanity becoming, at least in parts, more aware of the supernatural amongst them and normal humans taking up the hunt, basically it sounded like all the year of the hunter books taken together and expanded into a whole line about mortals confronting the supernatural. Imagine my disappointment when I got the book in my hands and immediately poured through it, there were no mortals in sight. These were supernatural beings who could detect other supernatural beings, and hear whispers or see text forming with orders for them to kill them, and the ability to call for example supernatural flames to surround their briefcase making it into a lethal weapon and despite all of this rather obvious display of supernatural power they still had the audacity to speak of themselves s humans and make the claim that the supernaturals were all evil, if that were the case they should have counted themselves amongst the evil ones as they were like said clearly supernatural themselves.<br /> <br /> I have no respect for these lousy supernatural serial killer wannabees, I reserve my respect for those mortals who despite the overwhelming odds decide to rise up against the supernatural with no supernatural protection from their powers and in many cases no weapons other than their wit's and whatever they may find handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T22:41:01-08:00","id":364130,"title":"","content":"Possessed...i think the idea of hunter is that &quot;The Guys Above&quot; realized that Humans by themselves woudnt be able to Stand a Chance..<br /> <br /> Now as for hunters being supernatural, i think it came because the rest of the WoD was getting too overpower for mere humans.<br /> Second...Theres internal grudges among hunters, theres those who belive that supernatural ISNT NESESARY EVIL they are called Innocents and Redeemers.<br /> <br /> Also, as for them hunting each other? Do you know what a Wayward Is?.<br /> one of the catches of the game is &quot;He who hunts monsters.&quot;<br /> also, if i were you, i would take a look to Bystander Hunters within HtR","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T22:42:38-08:00","id":364131,"title":"","content":"I don't even compare them since they exist to tell two very, very different stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T01:32:41-08:00","id":364181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364087#post364087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all the imbued are not &quot;hunters&quot; they are just slightly weaker bunch of supernatural creatures who are manipulated by stronger bunch of supernatural creatures,...</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, most of the Hunters Hunted organizations aren't hunters either, because they're slightly weaker supernaturals often being manipulated by stronger supernaturals to target their preferred enemies.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum is noted to have many Numina users (mostly hedge magicians) in their ranks and their leader is mysteriously special (aka not much of a spoiler that he's more than human + maybe some extra stuff.<br /> The NSA is often manipulated by the Technocracy (along with most of the other government organizations) and is responsible for helping create the technology that makes Orpheus possible. Psychic Numina are often present in government agents that deal with the supernatural.<br /> The Children of Osiris are a vampire Bloodline.<br /> The Society of Leopold are also Numina users and despite the Inquisition's efforts are constantly dealing with supernaturals manipulating the Church..<br /> The Shih are chi-using wuxia badasses.<br /> Strike Force Zero used cybernetics is manipulated by the Asian Technocracy.<br /> Dauntain manage to wield Banality (aka supernatural power) as a weapon against changelings.<br /> The Young Bloods are ghouls.<br /> The Knights of St. George use Numina.<br /> The Judges do as well.<br /> <br /> The idea that HtR isn't about hunters because the Imbued have powers, while the Hunters Hunted/Year of the Hunter books are about real human hunters is kind of ridiculous.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> As for the OP:<br /> <br /> I'm with Kirby that the two approaches are both for very different things. The HH approach largely deals with organizations that have experience and resources to hunt supernaturals with. It provides a more stable in-character structure because even if you're the fresh recruit that just say a supernatural for the first time, you have all that to fall back on to help. The HtR approach is best of hunters coming out of seemingly no where to figure out how to handle what's happened to them. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T04:17:44-08:00","id":364201,"title":"","content":"I like them both. I like the hunters from HH and the various splats with the Shih being my favourite of all time, but i love the Imbued. It feels like Buffy in the OWOD, and the Exalted easter eggs are the cherry on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T05:06:09-08:00","id":364250,"title":"","content":"Except for Inquisitor, I like them both. Part of the issue with most of the Year of the Hunter books is that most of those humans standing against the darkness where either manipulated or secretly run by supernatural masterminds.<br /> <br /> So I kind of liked the idea of scattered cells of random individuals with a sort of divine mandate, but it not being perfect/infallible protection nor clear what the right thing is. <br /> <br /> In the end, I liked that it was angels, but at the same time I kind of wish it had not been answered. I think both (really all) the lines offered different things to use and play. Not sure there is a huge issue mixing them up a bit. Each has advantages and disadvantages, though HtR clearly offered a lot more depth to setting and RP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T06:00:42-08:00","id":364277,"title":"","content":"Yeah while HH hunter organizations are minor supernatural templates, aka Numina users mostly, they are still mortal enough to be able to Awaken, be turned into a Vampire, go through the first change or Chrysalis (if Kinfolk/Kinain in which case their already minor supernaturals basically even if they don't know it and have zero powers) and if they die they can become Wraiths etc. They are mortal for all intents and purposes and have no particular Mary Sue resistance against the powers of those they hunt. Reckoning Hunters are a full on supernatural template with superior resistance to the powers of those they hunt and complete inability to ever become another template, just like other full templates have.<br /> <br /> Only exemption to the above are Dauntain and Children of Osiris both of which I leave out when speaking of Hunters as they are not hunters they are full on supernatural Templates.<br /> <br /> What I expected from the advertising back in the day was mortals rising up against the supernatural, a full on game line about why Vampires have the Masquerade, the Changers keep up the veil and so on. These were not created to hide from other supernaturals they were created to hide from the throngs of humanity which while out-powered individually still have the numbers to wage and win a war against the supernatural especially in the modern times with modern technology. This is what I would have loved the Reckoning to have been, that is what it was advertised to be. Instead we got another supernatural template. But considering that if I want to play a supernaturally empowered hunter I can always go Mage so Reckoning hunters really have no actual reason to exists, they are in fact perhaps even less mortals than Mages are considering they are pretty much unable to succumb to most mortal weaknesses that bind even the Mages, like Blood Bonds, Dominate, Embrace, becoming a Wraith after death etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i think the idea of hunter is that &quot;The Guys Above&quot; realized that Humans by themselves woudnt be able to Stand a Chance.. </div> </div> </div>And that thought is poisonous to the idea behind the other game lines. Masquerade is in place because Vampires know that should humanity rise against them they would likely win due to superior numbers alone and modern weaponry makes them even more dangerous. Similarly about the Veil, without it humanity could arm themselves with silver and could due to outnumbering the Garou by millions be able to hunt them to near extinction. Humanity does not need outside help to stand a chance and that is the whole idea of WoD all they need is to open their eyes and gather their courage.<br /> <br /> I've heard that Hunter the Vigil for nWoD might be more what I expected HtR to be but since I very much disliked the nWoD 1st edition system I have not yet delved too much into it rather awaiting 2nd edition of it though it did have a sort of update to GMC in Mortal Remains so it is likely not much of a priority to get a new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T07:42:10-08:00","id":364386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364087#post364087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wish Reckoning and everything associated with it would burn in eternal hell-fire and never be heard from again.<br /> <br /> So the answer is I'd prefer the Hunters that are presented in Hunters Hunted and other year of the hunter products. After all the imbued are not &quot;hunters&quot; they are just slightly weaker bunch of supernatural creatures who are manipulated by stronger bunch of supernatural creatures, that book if anything was about false advertising and remains only WoD line that I have sold all the books away from, and not because of monetary gain but just to get rid of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is the limit of your taste for a unified World of Darkness, is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:21:04-08:00","id":364466,"title":"","content":"In both NWoD and Hunter's Hunter there are a lot of groups that are part to mostly supernatural. Vigil definitely supports the &quot;no powers&quot; side of things a lot better than most anything in CWOD.<br /> <br /> I like having both Reckoning and the other groups around. I don't see any problem with Reckoning hunters being supernatural beings, but I do admit that that was a big part of my initial resistance to buying into the game. I got over it. Ran Reckoning a little bit. It is GRIM. But that's not bad if that's what you're going for. It was a lot darker than Hunter's Hunted style games I've been in. Hell, it was grimmer than our Wraith games. At least death was a mostly clean break. In Reckoning you get to watch people slowly lose everything they love and care about for a fight they end up having to chose or die or both. <br /> <br /> Plus, it seemed like Reckoning was a way to play a game with a Buffy-style character in it.<br /> <br /> I did largely purge Reckoning books to make space. I got rid of all the supes books. I just ran vampires as per Masquerade, werewolves as per Apocalypse, etc. I DID keep First Contact for the interactions with the other Hunters Hunted splats. I thought they were pretty interesting and fun. And built up the possibilities of Buffy-like games as well... so we have a Hedge Mage, a Hunter, a member of the Arcanum, and normal guy with a few others sprinkled in along the way,,, a NSA type, another Hedge Witch, a couple of ex-supes, a garou ronin or Child of Gaia who just kept that stuff off camera , etc.) Also, the place to get the juicy low down on what happened to the Orphic Circle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:47:26-08:00","id":364501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364277#post364277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are mortal for all intents and purposes and have no particular Mary Sue resistance against the powers of those they hunt. Reckoning Hunters are a full on supernatural template with superior resistance to the powers of those they hunt and complete inability to ever become another template, just like other full templates have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more than a tad of an exaggeration.<br /> <br /> The resistance granted by the Second Sight power is not passsive/permanent. It's an activated power with a limited resource that does not regenerate on it's own. Running out of Conviction leaves an Imbued 100% lacking in any special resistance to mental powers (and it only applies to mind trick powers, it doesn't nothing to stop a werewolf from ripping you in half or a mage from fireballing you), and if they fall victim to those powers they can be very easily trapped at Conviction 0 for an indefinite amount of time. There's a story in one of the books where an Imbued runs out of Conviction, gets mind-whammied by a vampire and is stuck as a mind-controlled servant for months before she finally makes a mistake in his orders that causes him to be able to activate 2nd Sight again and snap out of it.<br /> <br /> And... this is the cWOD. There aren't &quot;templates&quot; with consistent baseline stacking rules like the nWOD. A mages and werewolves can be embraced (even if Garou have resistance to it and the results if successful suck). Some dead &quot;major&quot; supernaturals can turn into ghosts and/or spirits. Sam Haight happened. The fact that the Imbued don't turn into other splats doesn't mean squat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only exemption to the above are Dauntain and Children of Osiris both of which I leave out when speaking of Hunters as they are not hunters they are full on supernatural Templates. </div> </div> </div>Which is just hypocrisy. Either the Year of the Hunter/HH material is about your concept of what a hunter should be, or it isn't. It clearly isn't, but the evidence that shows this is ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I expected from the advertising back in the day was mortals rising up against the supernatural, a full on game line about why Vampires have the Masquerade, the Changers keep up the veil and so on. </div> </div> </div>You expectations weren't accurate? That's not the books fault. Lets look at the back cover blurb:<br /> <br /> &quot;Take Back the Night<br /> <br /> For centuries, supernatural powers have reigned, warring among themselves, culling the human herds and lashing out from the shadows. The creatures of the night have held court since before the dawn of history.<br /> <br /> Nothing lasts forever.<br /> <br /> From the throng of humanity, individuals emerge who know the truth. [They] know monsters exist. Enough is enough. The forces of darkness must pay their due.<br /> <br /> You are the reckoning!&quot;<br /> <br /> The key point here: &quot;...individuals emerge who know the truth.&quot; Not, &quot;the masses rise up against the supernatural.&quot; So the claim that it was advertised to be about mundane humans using numbers to beat up supernaturals is outright shown not to be the case on the cover. It's a book about special individuals before you even crack it open.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But considering that if I want to play a supernaturally empowered hunter I can always go Mage so Reckoning hunters really have no actual reason to exists,... </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. First off, they don't have to deal with all that Mage stuff. HtR isn't a game about Paradigm wars and flexible magic slinging. Mage does not work well for the sudden &quot;Holy Shit!&quot; factor that the Imbued deal with followed by being lost in a world full of monsters. If anything, Mage makes more of the YotH/HH groups irrelevant. You could easily play most of them as a linears only game (Government agents/DNA/SF0 = Technocrats, Shih = Akashics, a small tweak makes the Arcanum = Hermetics, the SoL = Templars/Chorus, etc.) focused on going around taking out other supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they are in fact perhaps even less mortals than Mages are considering they are pretty much unable to succumb to most mortal weaknesses that bind even the Mages, like Blood Bonds, Dominate, Embrace, becoming a Wraith after death etc. </div> </div> </div>That's a fairly myopic definition of things. Imbued can't live for centuries, bend reality to their whims, travel to other planes of existence, transform into legendary mythical creatures, etc. Hunters also don't have any power that lets them soak damage better; even if they have some healing powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've heard that Hunter the Vigil for nWoD might be more what I expected HtR to be but since I very much disliked the nWoD 1st edition system I have not yet delved too much into it rather awaiting 2nd edition of it though it did have a sort of update to GMC in Mortal Remains so it is likely not much of a priority to get a new edition. </div> </div> </div>Probably. Thought HtV is more HH than it is what you have said you wanted HtR to be. It's not about humanity rising up against the supernatural en masse. It's about groups of humans (and not so humans) ganging together against the more potent supernaturals out there.<br /> <br /> The one thing it has that probably would appeal to you is mechanical support for completely mortal hunters with no supernatural powers (they do have some advantages normal people don't) as well as hunters that have access to supernatural boosts (whether through collections of mystic artifacts, crazy science, or being born special, or whatever).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T11:24:39-08:00","id":364613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364466#post364466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In both NWoD and Hunter's Hunter there are a lot of groups that are part to mostly supernatural. Vigil definitely supports the &quot;no powers&quot; side of things a lot better than most anything in CWOD.<br /> <br /> I like having both Reckoning and the other groups around. I don't see any problem with Reckoning hunters being supernatural beings, but I do admit that that was a big part of my initial resistance to buying into the game. I got over it. Ran Reckoning a little bit. It is GRIM. But that's not bad if that's what you're going for. It was a lot darker than Hunter's Hunted style games I've been in. Hell, it was grimmer than our Wraith games. At least death was a mostly clean break. In Reckoning you get to watch people slowly lose everything they love and care about for a fight they end up having to chose or die or both.<br /> <br /> Plus, it seemed like Reckoning was a way to play a game with a Buffy-style character in it.<br /> <br /> I did largely purge Reckoning books to make space. I got rid of all the supes books. I just ran vampires as per Masquerade, werewolves as per Apocalypse, etc. I DID keep First Contact for the interactions with the other Hunters Hunted splats. I thought they were pretty interesting and fun. And built up the possibilities of Buffy-like games as well... so we have a Hedge Mage, a Hunter, a member of the Arcanum, and normal guy with a few others sprinkled in along the way,,, a NSA type, another Hedge Witch, a couple of ex-supes, a garou ronin or Child of Gaia who just kept that stuff off camera , etc.) Also, the place to get the juicy low down on what happened to the Orphic Circle...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it as Buffy. I see it as They Live, but with Hoffman Lenses that never quite fully come off. Also, a shot of Darker than Black. Granted, the second standpoint is one that's only possible long after the run of H:TR ended, but Hazuki Mina's power resembles Cleave, and Hei's electrical powers approach something like one of the more powerful Defense Edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T15:18:36-08:00","id":364818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Take Back the Night<br /> <br /> For centuries, supernatural powers have reigned, warring among themselves, culling the human herds and lashing out from the shadows. The creatures of the night have held court since before the dawn of history.<br /> <br /> Nothing lasts forever.<br /> <br /> From the throng of humanity, individuals emerge who know the truth. [They] know monsters exist. Enough is enough. The forces of darkness must pay their due.<br /> <br /> You are the reckoning!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Nothing in this says that those individuals are supernaturals themselves rather it implies that individual humans emerge knowing the truth.<br /> <br /> I see that you are unwilling to see my point, which is that I, and many many others over the years, had the expectation of humans rising against the supernatural and what we got was supernatural creatures rising against the supernatural. That HH has numina wielding hunters, which are in my opinion much more interesting than Reckonings hunters who wield even more supernatural power, is not the point I would have preferred HH to have been expanded into a line of it's own but even more I would have preferred the Reckoning line to have been about mortals rising from the throng of humanity knowing monsters exist, like surviving victims or relatives of those killed by the supernaturals, would have been infinitely more interesting and supportive of the themes of both hunters, as an idea in general, and the other lines as well. What Reckoning does is only enforce the image of helpless humanity which is like I said kinda poisonous to the themes of the other lines.<br /> <br /> Reckoning also robs the other lines from moral dilemmas normal mortals would have inflicted. Had the hunters been mortal victims of the supernatural who had enough it would have forced the supernaturals to look at themselves and their deeds even if they are forced to kill their hunters, which could be a moral dilemma in itself where as the Reckoning hunters being as they are clearly supernatural in origin it only makes them think about what supernatural power is conspiring against them this time, no reflection on their own actions. Just another bunch of supernaturals after them.<br /> <br /> But like said this is my opinion, which I know many share, and despite me wishing to see Reckoning purged from existence I do think it's fans deserve their chance of 20th edition when the time comes and it's not really away from me especially if those rumors about Vigil being what I wish are true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T15:41:25-08:00","id":364827,"title":"","content":"personally, i feel that reckoning was made because many Human players ended up against the ropes when it came to supernaturals. What can a human do against a Rank 4 Werewolf , or a 6th generation vampire? or a very old wraith?<br /> when it comes down, humans cant save themselves. and lets be honest, you can have a max stats human (no numina, no nothing), a fucking rambo. but if a fucking rambo has to take down something that can move through the umbra or do more than one action per turn, youre fucked up anyways. humans will always be the underdogs (on my opinion). the Edges made for the hunters were a way to Contrarest some of this powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T16:33:08-08:00","id":364893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364818#post364818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that you are unwilling to see my point, which is that I, and many many others over the years, had the expectation of humans rising against the supernatural and what we got was supernatural creatures rising against the supernatural. That HH has numina wielding hunters, which are in my opinion much more interesting than Reckonings hunters who wield even more supernatural power,</div> </div> </div> </div>You think instant empowerment that you have no fucking idea where it comes from is &quot;MORE&quot; outside the norm than Spending years living in a monster hunter village learning Kungfu, being a psychic member of a secret government agency? Being a member of a secret religious order who's very Faith burns vampires? These people are NORMAL. These people who don't have to deal with a job, family have backings more than a simpler internet room. Yeah they have as much in common with your average person as your average vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is not the point I would have preferred HH to have been expanded into a line of it's own but even more I would have preferred the Reckoning line to have been about mortals rising from the throng of humanity knowing monsters exist, like surviving victims or relatives of those killed by the supernaturals, would have been infinitely more interesting and supportive of the themes of both hunters, as an idea in general, and the other lines as well. What Reckoning does is only enforce the image of helpless humanity which is like I said kinda poisonous to the themes of the other lines. </div> </div> </div>How do you get a line from this? Why is this not BETTER served by books that actively cater to particular lines than some broad &quot;victim&quot; game?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reckoning also robs the other lines from moral dilemmas normal mortals would have inflicted. Had the hunters been mortal victims of the supernatural who had enough it would have forced the supernaturals to look at themselves and their deeds even if they are forced to kill their hunters, which could be a moral dilemma in itself where as the Reckoning hunters being as they are clearly supernatural in origin it only makes them think about what supernatural power is conspiring against them this time, no reflection on their own actions. Just another bunch of supernaturals after them. </div> </div> </div>HOW? Reckoning no more made every other hunter disappear than Werewolves invalidate Gangrel. They are crossover. It doesn't make Hunters Hunted, Inquisition, Arcanum, Project Twilight, Saviors and Destroyers etc disappear. Hell Saviors came out AFTER Reckoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But like said this is my opinion, which I know many share, and despite me wishing to see Reckoning purged from existence I do think it's fans deserve their chance of 20th edition when the time comes and it's not really away from me especially if those rumors about Vigil being what I wish are true. </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think you need to stop treating Reckoning as a replacement for what you want. Its not. Its itsown thing, about people being thrown in the deep end. It has alot of interesting story to tell but in no way invalidates what you want because it doesn't cover it at all. Demand a Hunter's Hunted for everyline. That would give you what you want and allow you to cater to particular stories than have things get watered down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T17:40:35-08:00","id":364921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly I think you need to stop treating Reckoning as a replacement for what you want. </div> </div> </div>I have years ago in fact. That is why I sold away my HtR books like I told earlier. I was asked why I dislike HtR and I answered it and I know there are plenty of people who agree with me just as I know there are plenty of people who disagree with me.<br /> <br /> Of course HtR doesn't make all the other hunters disappear, and even if it did it wouldn't at my table, but what it did was overshadow them and that was a shame.<br /> <br /> Also one of my grief's was the advertisement of the line when it was coming. Everyone thought back then that it was about mortals rising up right until they read the book.<br /> <br /> Point is if your fan of the line we are not gonna meat eye to eye on this matter. There is nothing you can say to sway me to like these supernatural beings more and I cannot say anything that would sway you from liking them and now were just stealing a thread.<br /> <br /> Still as a last note this particular theme<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its itsown thing, about people being thrown in the deep end. </div> </div> </div>can easily be played out in Mage as Orphans, in Vampire as Caitiff and in Werewolf as a lost cub. They are all thrown in the deep end the Orphan Mage being so close to hunter it almost blurs the line. They have mysterious voices or even visitations that try to guide them, Avatar, have just been shoved supernatural powers out of the blue, in 2nd edition this could be a from an close call encounter with a supernatural for example etc.<br /> <br /> But like I said this is kinda pointless isn't it. If you like Hunter do so, if you don't, don't.<br /> <br /> For those who like it I do hope you get your chance at a kickstarter for 20th anniversary edition but like said previously it has nothing to offer me hence I just won't be part of it. Simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T18:08:49-08:00","id":364943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364181#post364181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case, most of the Hunters Hunted organizations aren't hunters either, because they're slightly weaker supernaturals often being manipulated by stronger supernaturals to target their preferred enemies.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum is noted to have many Numina users (mostly hedge magicians) in their ranks and their leader is mysteriously special (aka not much of a spoiler that he's more than human + maybe some extra stuff.<br /> The NSA is often manipulated by the Technocracy (along with most of the other government organizations) and is responsible for helping create the technology that makes Orpheus possible. Psychic Numina are often present in government agents that deal with the supernatural.<br /> The Children of Osiris are a vampire Bloodline.<br /> The Society of Leopold are also Numina users and despite the Inquisition's efforts are constantly dealing with supernaturals manipulating the Church..<br /> The Shih are chi-using wuxia badasses.<br /> Strike Force Zero used cybernetics is manipulated by the Asian Technocracy.<br /> Dauntain manage to wield Banality (aka supernatural power) as a weapon against changelings.<br /> The Young Bloods are ghouls.<br /> The Knights of St. George use Numina.<br /> The Judges do as well.<br /> <br /> The idea that HtR isn't about hunters because the Imbued have powers, while the Hunters Hunted/Year of the Hunter books are about real human hunters is kind of ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh God, this is perfect.<br /> <br /> I like all the Hunter books that White Wolf, and now Onyx Path, have released. But between the two, I prefer to play Reckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T18:15:08-08:00","id":364948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364921#post364921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can easily be played out in Mage as Orphans, in Vampire as Caitiff and in Werewolf as a lost cub. They are all thrown in the deep end the Orphan Mage being so close to hunter it almost blurs the line. They have mysterious voices or even visitations that try to guide them, Avatar, have just been shoved supernatural powers out of the blue, in 2nd edition this could be a from an close call encounter with a supernatural for example etc.<br /> <br /> But like I said this is kinda pointless isn't it. If you like Hunter do so, if you don't, don't.<br /> <br /> For those who like it I do hope you get your chance at a kickstarter for 20th anniversary edition but like said previously it has nothing to offer me hence I just won't be part of it. Simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And One can play out &quot;Werewolf&quot; with gangrel. Mage with Tremere etc. Why have any game other then Vampire the Masquerade? Yes you can hammer things into a different slot. No, its not the same as having a game customized about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T18:24:42-08:00","id":364954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364818#post364818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But like said this is my opinion, which <u>I know many share</u>,</b><br /> <br /> <b>For those who like it I do hope you get your chance at a kickstarter for 20th anniversary edition but like said previously it has nothing to offer me hence I just won't be part of it. Simple as that.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you continue to type this? I don't get it. I feel like you repeat this comment in every single thread about Reckoning.<br /> <br /> I could just as easily state how many people share my opinion that Hunter the Reckoning is a fantastic game about <b>humans with abilities that are able to fight back</b> against the monsters that plague the night.<br /> <br /> Hunters from Reckoning are just as human as Captain America. Humans that can easily be killed, but with some special skills that enable them to fight back. They are still JUST AS fragile as normal humans. You don't like it? Cool. But why venture into almost every thread about Reckoning and shout out about how much you hate it and everyone you know hates it. We get it. I promise you. Everyone here gets it.<br /> <br /> he game line sold quite well, from what I understand. Even got 3 videogames out of it. Sorry.<br /> <br /> To me, it sounds like you are mad that you got something different than you expected. Which, as Heavy Arms pointed out, was not really what was advertised.<br /> <br /> White Wolf advertised the game about normal humans, given powers called edges, to help fight back against the forces of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> What we got was a game about normal humans, given powers called edges, that they used to fight back against the forces of the supernatural. And they are human. Human, human, human.<br /> <br /> I don't want to play a story where I play an Orphan from Mage.<br /> <br /> I want to play a story where I'm fighting against bloodsuckers at 3am in the morning, and four hours from then, I have to be awake for a college course in European history, while balancing a girlfriend, and working as a life guard at the local beach during the daytime.<br /> <br /> Reckoning allows me to do this. Don't allow other people's fun to impede on your own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-09-2015, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T20:21:55-08:00","id":365050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=364818#post364818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that you are unwilling to see my point, which is that I, and many many others over the years, had the expectation of humans rising against the supernatural and what we got was supernatural creatures rising against the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that &quot;I had expectations that were not met&quot; only goes so far as a criticism. It's certainly not a criticism of the game itself. There's also little to no evidence that the expectation was reasonable. The early advertising might not have explicitly sold HtR as what it was, but it didn't explicitly sell it as what you wanted either.<br /> <br /> Ultimately your expectations are something you create for yourself. If there was some serious misleading advertising on WW's part back when HtR was in the works, your point would be better received. The lack of that makes your point hard to take seriously. &quot;HtR should die in a fire because I lied to myself,&quot; is not compelling, and it makes everything else your write about it (especially the stuff that doesn't hold up to logical scrutiny) sound like sour grapes rather than useful insight into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reckoning also robs the other lines from moral dilemmas normal mortals would have inflicted. Had the hunters been mortal victims of the supernatural who had enough it would have forced the supernaturals to look at themselves and their deeds even if they are forced to kill their hunters, which could be a moral dilemma in itself where as the Reckoning hunters being as they are clearly supernatural in origin it only makes them think about what supernatural power is conspiring against them this time, no reflection on their own actions. Just another bunch of supernaturals after them. </div> </div> </div>1) The &quot;mortal hunter born of supernatural abuse&quot; still exists in the WOD with or without the Imbued. This moral dilemma doesn't go away just because some hunters have powers.<br /> <br /> 2) Supernaturals have minimal ways of knowing what the Imbued are. Most Edges aren't obvious. The long standing existence of hunters with minor powers means that there's no reason to assume the Imbued are something else. The Imbued have a clearly supernatural origin to us, as readers, not to characters in the universe. <br /> <br /> 3) This is another point that runs into a giant logical consistency problem. The cWOD game lines are horrible about running over each other. Crossover always has issues with the themes and metaphysics of one game clashing with those of the other(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T20:54:57-08:00","id":365064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want to play a story where I'm fighting against bloodsuckers at 3am in the morning, and four hours from then, I have to be awake for a college course in European history, while balancing a girlfriend, and working as a life guard at the local beach during the daytime. </div> </div> </div>All possible things for an Orphan Mage as well. Just check Orphan survival guide and you'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't allow other people's fun to impede on your own. </div> </div> </div>I don't. Like I said multiple times this ain't happening at my table but I do not deny it from those who enjoy it, unlike many KotE haters I aren't even trying to deny you your earned 20th anniversary edition. On the contrary if the kickstarters goes online I'll wish you the best but just won't participate in it myself. It's not away from me, it's just a game line I dislike immensely.<br /> <br /> And again I would have left this thread at my first post had Crowley not asked me to clarify my stance. Why do I continue to mention that this is not only my opinion is because it is not as some defenders here try to implicate me for both misattributing the advertisement of the line and other such things even though as recently as the last forum there used to be huge wars about this very subject and I haven't likely even taken part in half of them. I seem to even remember a thread locked about this when things got out of hand, to my relief it was one thread that I had the sense to stay out from the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters from Reckoning are just as human as Captain America. </div> </div> </div>The old Captain is superhuman, you know he took a super soldier serum don't ya. And he survived after freezing over in the ocean feeling ok being smelted down 60 years later so he really is pretty damn far from being as fragile as humans are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> why venture into almost every thread about Reckoning </div> </div> </div>I think I have done somewhat well in staying out of HtR threads during this incarnation of the forums haven't I? I thought so at least, could be wrong though. Still this thread was and is specifically about which currently existing hunter type everyone prefers and I came to tell my opinion and like I said above then asked to clarify that opinion further. Then people came in and drew me further into this, and I admit I could have just left few posts ago but sometimes one cannot help one self and you just wish to try to clarify your point. In the hopes of reaching at the least a level of both understanding each others stance, but I see now that it seem somewhat impossible. I really do not see what new or great HtR brought to the table and those who like it won't recede even the point of it's poor advertisement, and that's a first in every other argument over the years no one has ever tried to defend that those misleading things would have implicated anything else than humans as protagonists, let alone the fact that it has very little differences thematically from playing Orphaned Magi who try to cope with their powers on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can a human do against a Rank 4 Werewolf , or a 6th generation vampire? or a very old wraith? </div> </div> </div>Rank 4 or not if surprised they don't soak silver any better than at Rank 1. 6th Gen is likely somewhat older Vampire and so likely lower on his Road/Path/Humanity thus being perhaps even weaker than most during the day which is the time to strike for any sensible Vampire hunter, stake, sunlight or fire or all three safest is usually just to add gasoline over and around the sleeping thing and fire it up. Wraith I gotta hand to you unless you have some necromantic mojo and he is proficient with cross Shroud Arcanoi your screwed no matter what critter you are.<br /> <br /> But like said each to his own, you like reckoning good for you I hope you the best. I do not have to like the game for you to enjoy it so how about we drop this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T21:26:22-08:00","id":365098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365064#post365064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All possible things for an Orphan Mage as well. Just check Orphan survival guide and you'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I can play someone who turns into a wolf who protects the forest with Gangrel. Why have werewolf? I can play occult mystery with Tremere, why have Mages? You readily defend KOTE(&quot;Why not just do it with Kindred&quot;) that you are basically using here against Hunters. Orphan mages are NOT customized for the premise. I mean Paradox is a big thing in Mage afterall, could you bend the game for that? Absolutely. Could I run a game about wolf changers with vampire? yes. Does that make them applicable? No","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T21:46:51-08:00","id":365105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365098#post365098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And I can play someone who turns into a wolf who protects the forest with Gangrel. Why have werewolf? I can play occult mystery with Tremere, why have Mages? You readily defend KOTE(&quot;Why not just do it with Kindred&quot;) that you are basically using here against Hunters. Orphan mages are NOT customized for the premise. I mean Paradox is a big thing in Mage afterall, could you bend the game for that? Absolutely. Could I run a game about wolf changers with vampire? yes. Does that make them applicable? No</div> </div> </div> </div>For the KotE part I know and acknowledge it in another thread I am not oblivious to my own doings you know. And unlike many who have an issue with KotE I am not trying to convince anyone of replacing HtR and I'm certainly not trying to advertise the idea that fans of HtR shouldn't get their chance of gaining a 20th anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> Gangrel and werewolf are several spirit worlds apart from each other. So that is not really a valid comparison. Tremere and Mages get closer but again Tremre are somewhat more limited than mages, only night time, no spirit worlds etc. For KotE why not Kindred? Because they have been established as something else it is already canon and the line sold as well as hunter, or at least it has as many books as hunter.<br /> <br /> Orphan Mages differ from HtR hunters in that they have more potential power to be gained and that they have to deal with Paradox and naturally they are not actively encouraged to fight other supernaturals by the voices they hear. But could they be played out as hunters easily. Paradox could manifest as Quiet leading them down the same slippery road towards madness that hunter sometimes go. They are as squishy as hunters and without Mind Sphere easier to influence. So it is not actually that far fetched but like said if you like hunter good for you.<br /> <br /> Happy with the answers? Could we now drop this as it starts to feel like were stealing this thread away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T21:50:14-08:00","id":365107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365064#post365064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All possible things for an Orphan Mage as well. Just check Orphan survival guide and you'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one here wants to. Why should they? &quot;You can do anything with Mage!&quot; is among the least helpful technically true statements there is in the hobby for people not particularly invested in Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rank 4 or not if surprised they don't soak silver any better than at Rank 1. </div> </div> </div>Does the athro have Luna's Armor active when this hypothetical surprise occurs? If so, then yes, this character is indeed better at soaking silver than a cliath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T21:57:06-08:00","id":365110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365107#post365107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one here wants to. Why should they? &quot;You can do anything with Mage!&quot; is among the least helpful technically true statements there is in the hobby for people not particularly invested in Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does the athro have Luna's Armor active when this hypothetical surprise occurs? If so, then yes, this character is indeed better at soaking silver than a cliath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not saying you can do anything with Mage but just that Oprhans are just what the poster there described hunters as, normal people who are thrown into the deep end with no guidance and sudden supernatural abilities. So it's a pretty valid comparison as that is what was claimed to make HtR different from other lines.<br /> <br /> Well does the athro keep Luna'a Armor active at all times if yes then you are correct if only when expecting trouble then it's obviously not on that is the whole point of surprise attacks to catch the quarry unprepared. If a prepared for combat does it really matter whether the enemy is Imbued or mortal? Not really as the athro is more than capable of ripping either apart along with their friends in seconds.<br /> <br /> Since no one seems interested in dropping the matter please let's stop using this thread and PM me if your interested in continuation of this rather pointless conversation I shall indulge you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T22:50:39-08:00","id":365124,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose I really get the point of arguing with Possessed (you guys aren't really discussing anything). He doesn't like HtR because it isn't what he thought it would or should be. No big deal.That has nothing to do with whether or not anyone else can enjoy it.<br /> <br /> That being said, I've played in both HH games and HtR and both had their ups and downs. The HH game was more difficult I think since anytime someone screwed up, even the littlest bit someone died (or worse). The HtR game had a bit more leeway since edges can save your ass. It isn't just the &quot;didn't roll high enough on stealth so the werewolf spots you. He goes crinos, you're Willpower isn't high enough so you're dead without a fighting chance&quot;. At least the HtR you get second sight to act as a buffer. Just my opinion though. both games have their strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T23:03:09-08:00","id":365129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365105#post365105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the KotE part I know and acknowledge it in another thread I am not oblivious to my own doings you know. And unlike many who have an issue with KotE I am not trying to convince anyone of replacing HtR and I'm certainly not trying to advertise the idea that fans of HtR shouldn't get their chance of gaining a 20th anniversary edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet you keep saying the Orphan thing as if its a truism. <br /> <br /> {quote]Gangrel and werewolf are several spirit worlds apart from each other.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Hunter and Orphans are miles apart thematically. Give Gangrel Spiritus and some magic. Bam.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So that is not really a valid comparison. </div> </div> </div>vague superficial visuals are enough for you to keep bringing up Orphans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere and Mages get closer but again Tremre are somewhat more limited than mages, only night time, no spirit worlds etc. </div> </div> </div>Orphans are some what more limited than Hunters having Paradox lack of innate protection against various supernatural powers, having a System built internally on belief vs external factors.<br /> <br /> <br /> For KotE why not Kindred? Because they have been established as<br /> something else it is already canon and the line sold as well as hunter, or at least it has as many books as hunter.<br /> <br /> {quote]Orphan Mages differ from HtR hunters in that they have more potential power to be gained and that they have to deal with Paradox and naturally they are not actively encouraged to fight other supernaturals by the voices they hear. But could they be played out as hunters easily. Paradox could manifest as Quiet leading them down the same slippery road towards madness that hunter sometimes go. They are as squishy as hunters and without Mind Sphere easier to influence. So it is not actually that far fetched but like said if you like hunter good for you.<br /> <br /> .[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> And I can use a Screwdriver for a hammer. A hammer is a better tool for hitting nails. That I could completely build another game with another game Orphans do not cover the same category UNILESS you force it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T23:47:32-08:00","id":365173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365124#post365124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose I really get the point of arguing with Possessed (you guys aren't really discussing anything). He doesn't like HtR because it isn't what he thought it would or should be. No big deal.That has nothing to do with whether or not anyone else can enjoy it.<br /> <br /> That being said, I've played in both HH games and HtR and both had their ups and downs. The HH game was more difficult I think since anytime someone screwed up, even the littlest bit someone died (or worse). The HtR game had a bit more leeway since edges can save your ass. It isn't just the &quot;didn't roll high enough on stealth so the werewolf spots you. He goes crinos, you're Willpower isn't high enough so you're dead without a fighting chance&quot;. At least the HtR you get second sight to act as a buffer. Just my opinion though. both games have their strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting for truth. Thank you for understanding what I have been trying to say for a few posts already.<br /> <br /> Lian for you I'd like to quote something as well since you obviously didn't get it perhaps repetition is the key to learning.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since no one seems interested in dropping the matter <u><i><b>please let's stop using this thread and PM me if your interested in continuation of this rather pointless conversation I shall indulge you there.</b></i></u> </div> </div> </div>This time I kinda thought that perhaps I should emphasize the important part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T02:15:23-08:00","id":365225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365124#post365124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose I really get the point of arguing with Possessed (you guys aren't really discussing anything). He doesn't like HtR because it isn't what he thought it would or should be. No big deal.That has nothing to do with whether or not anyone else can enjoy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not, and I don't think most of the others responding to him, are actually trying to convince him to like the game. What we're doing is calling him on all the BS he's spewing because for some reason he can't actually leave is opinion as, &quot;[Possessed] doesn't like HtR because it isn't what he thought it would or should be.&quot; If that's all he said there wouldn't be all this.<br /> <br /> If you don't like something simply as a matter of preference, people don't tend to argue with you about it. People can ask why, but why is a fairly easy question to avoid on a forum. &quot;It's a personal thing, I don't feel like talking about it.&quot; I've run into very few people on forums (and even less that don't get banned fairly quickly) that can't drop it then<br /> <br /> The problem is when you start justifying why you don't like something. I really don't like CtD as it stands. In threads where I discuss this, I'm prepared to go into quite some detail about it. And when I say something about the books, I make a good faith effort to be accurate about them. When I say the mechanics annoy me, I can point to solid examples (the Glamour regaining systems, Banality assignments, switching Seemings). If I just sat around slinging around mud with no critical analysis, I think CtD fans would be well within their right to call me on it, and debunk what I was saying so people curious about the game aren't just listening to me ranting about it.<br /> <br /> And that comes into why I've continued to respond to Possessed's points. It's not really for Possessed to &quot;see the light&quot; about HtR, but to call the grossly inaccurate things posted in defense of their justification for disliking it out for being such. It's also why I have no interest in taking it to PMs either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T03:01:43-08:00","id":365238,"title":"","content":"I've never liked HtR, the concept just felt off for me and for some of the reasons Possessed has given. They were just another supernatural splat shoehorned into what always felt like a /the Crossover slot between the main lines. Now before I get a reiteration of how supernatural the other Hunter stuff was I;d like to point out that since the very beginning of the WoD (or close enough) we've been told that mortals are Mortals but some of them learn bits of the truth and try to bring down the monsters that ruined their lives, killed their friends or they are ordered to by shadowy organisations (Inquisition) but we've also been told that some mortals a rare few (and typically those that end up interacting with the supernatural) know a few tricks of their own (Numina and a few of the merits that were out there). For the longest time the best weapon against Vampires was faith, as in True Faith, that was the Mortal's go to for being a Vampire Hunter and it meshed perfectly with the setting. It also fitted nicely into Werewolf as well where we also saw a few more Numina amongst the Kinfolk and Mage did have it's Sorcerers. But suffice to say we'd been given plenty of evidence and a few small supplement books that told us what mortals were in the world of darkness and that yes you didn't have to be a supernatural &quot;splat&quot; to be able to tweak a little power to help close the odds by a few inches (and that's all that Numina and Faith gave you, Psychic Void was a little nastier). <br /> <br /> The other thing we'd been told about through Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and Wraith was that being a Hunter required a lot of planning, learning and absolute luck, otherwise you're dead, Playing a Hunter was likely to be a brief brutal experience because even if you had Faith or had learned some of the secret truths of the world to use on your side you were up against things that were vastly more powerful than you, that was the point and odds are you were doing it for some form of personal reason (a la Punisher). So for years this is what we had learned Hunters within the WoD to be. They were mortals who existed very much in the cracks of the WoD. <br /> <br /> HtR which was meant to be the Hunters game didn't mesh with any of this. I'm not referring to what could or couldn't be done with it but the core default of how it's presented and put together. It wasn't about True Faith, Lucky and maybe the ability to heal someone else of 2 levels of lethal damage. It wasn't about having enough WP to hold out on the Delirium well enough to still be able to act. It wasn't about tracking down journals and documents to learn about Vampiric Clan flaws or risking your life to talk with a Ghoul who might let something slip or trying to find just enough silver to bring down that Shapeshifter. It wasn't about stakeouts to work out if so and so really was a creature of the night or just kept an odd routine to their lives. Sure some of the things you could pick up as a mortal could get around fragments of that part of the game but even the Templar faith magic from DaC that let you see a supernatural only worked in a full on conversation with them and then was limited to by type. Nope. HtR was a VERY different game it how it appeared and was presented (even played). Worse still the way it was put together that the Imbued came to be sounded very very similar to an Avatar awakening in many respects which would make them not Imbued but Mages. Note that I know that HtR games could and certainly did involve sometimes some of the above but the sheer life or death, success or failure necessity of it was removed from the feel of the game. <br /> <br /> Remove it from the rest of the WoD and it was fine as a Stand Alone (just like we played the other line anyway all so often) but put into a Crossover perspective (where the Hunter concept often sat alongside it's mortal origins) and it simply didn't sit well. Ironically the biggest complaint I heard in some circles (typically in the online chat games) was how that the Imbued were typically weaker than the other Supernatural splats. It was a game line that had stepped over the old concept of hunters to bring in a new funky concept of hunter that was a supernatural creature imbued with powers to bring down the other supernatural creatures of the WoD for 'reasons' that one on one were often not capable of fulfilling that function. Yes it felt a little like a Buffy type attempt that wasn't as good as the licensed property doing the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T04:02:45-08:00","id":365291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365238#post365238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for putting most of my complaints in a more neutral tone and explaining once more what my point is and was. Thank you, while my general anger at the line, and at how this thread progressed, likely prevented me from framing my point as elegantly as you did, this is exactly my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T04:23:48-08:00","id":365316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365238#post365238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now before I get a reiteration of how supernatural the other Hunter stuff was I;d like to point out that since the very beginning of the WoD (or close enough) we've been told that mortals are Mortals but some of them learn bits of the truth and try to bring down the monsters...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, you're going to get it anyway.<br /> <br /> There is no logically consistent way to say that a Sorcerer is not a supernatural &quot;creature&quot; but an Imbued is. Either having powers makes you a supernatural, in which case all Numina users are supernaturals, even True Faith ones, or simply having powers is not what makes a character a supernatural critter at which point there's no solid case that the Imbued are anything other than a new type of Numina user with funky rules.<br /> <br /> The cWOD has always presented the hunters of the supernatural as people that end up blurring the lines between mortal and supernatural in order to gain the power they need to fight back. HtR is no different in this regard. Drawing an arbitrary line between the Imbued and the hunters presented in other books that use special powers is just that; an arbitrary line. It's only purpose is to try to make a personal preference look like something based in fact instead of just being a personal preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HtR which was meant to be the Hunters game didn't mesh with any of this. I'm not referring to what could or couldn't be done with it but the core default of how it's presented and put together. It wasn't about True Faith, Lucky and maybe the ability to heal someone else of 2 levels of lethal damage. It wasn't about having enough WP to hold out on the Delirium well enough to still be able to act. </div> </div> </div>Because it uses different systems? It's about being lucky and hoping you have enough Conviction instead of Faith or Willpower. Yes, it isn't about faith. It's about commitment. Because it isn't trying to be Hunter: the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It wasn't about tracking down journals and documents to learn about Vampiric Clan flaws or risking your life to talk with a Ghoul who might let something slip or trying to find just enough silver to bring down that Shapeshifter. </div> </div> </div>Odd.... HtR presents this as a very common thing. It has come up in every HtR game I've ever played. Even with short-cut Edges out there to make some of this go faster (like being able to figure out supernatural weaknesses more easily), you still have to figure out how to capitalize on them. Hunters don't have a magical power to generate real fire (only does lethal by default instead of Agg, even in crossover), wooden stakes, holy relics, silver, or whatever you end up needing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It wasn't about stakeouts to work out if so and so really was a creature of the night or just kept an odd routine to their lives. </div> </div> </div>Yep, this it does short cut around. The stake outs are for figuring out what you're going to do about it; which is very clearly stated in the books as the bigger focus of the game. It's not a investigation mystery focused game. It's about figuring out what your character would do now that they know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HtR was a VERY different game it how it appeared and was presented (even played). </div> </div> </div>How does, &quot;HtR is very different from the previous hunter focused books,&quot; get to, &quot;it is internally incoherent?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or do you mean, &quot;HtR is different from the other hunters.&quot; Which was always the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worse still the way it was put together that the Imbued came to be sounded very very similar to an Avatar awakening in many respects which would make them not Imbued but Mages. </div> </div> </div>Eh? Only superficially. Getting Imbued is a sudden epiphany moment, in a moment of mortal peril. Awakening can be that, and dozens of other things. The only similarity is that they can both be suddenly seeing the truth. That's not what makes an Imbued or a Mage alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that I know that HtR games could and certainly did involve sometimes some of the above but the sheer life or death, success or failure necessity of it was removed from the feel of the game. </div> </div> </div>I've seen more PC deaths in HtR than I have in ever other cWOD game I've played combined excluded Werewolf (which is a pretty high lethality game if you want it to be).<br /> <br /> The Imbued have zero protections from damage besides body armor. They might be able to avoid harm, and some can recover fast, but they are not tanks in a world where anyone can deal a lot of damage. One of the easiest ways to kill an Imbued is to just mind-whammy a mortal into doing it for you (or paying them if you have that open to you) since very few of their powers work against mortal or mundane stuff. Guns do wonders against the Imbued. There's pretty much nothing the Imbued can do about a sniper they don't see, or a car bomb, or a cut brake line, etc.<br /> <br /> Besides be paranoid and be really good at planning and strategy... which you are saying they don't need to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remove it from the rest of the WoD and it was fine as a Stand Alone (just like we played the other line anyway all so often) but put into a Crossover perspective (where the Hunter concept often sat alongside it's mortal origins) and it simply didn't sit well. </div> </div> </div>Which could be said of any of the cWOD games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ironically the biggest complaint I heard in some circles (typically in the online chat games) was how that the Imbued were typically weaker than the other Supernatural splats. </div> </div> </div>Because they are. Their powers are fairly low level, they get very few of them, and they can't buy them with XP. They earn powers with the same currency they use to activate them. Also their 4 dot powers are behind having to have four permanent and untreatable derangements, and can only be taken if you are willing to give up on lots of other Edges (to get three 4 dot Edges, one per Virtue, you need all Virtues at 10, 12 derangements, and you only get 12 powers total out of the deal, all of which have to be from the same path). Numina users don't have to jump through that many hoops to get to 4 dots in a Path... they can start with that. And they can buy up as many as they like without mechanical penalties or caps. 5th dot Edge? You get one, maybe, and it's even more worth to get at. And they are nothing compared to having 5 dots in a Discipline or worse the 5th dot of a Sphere.<br /> <br /> As mentioned, they also have zero soak/damage negation powers. Don't have Ward? Sorry, but most Garou are going to gut you in the first round despite your fancy immunity to Delirium. Have Ward? Ok, they just use their superhuman strength to throw things at you instead. Or use a bow or a gun if they're they type to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was a game line that had stepped over the old concept of hunters to bring in a new funky concept of hunter... </div> </div> </div>Um... yeah? That's sort of the point isn't it? Why would HtR not be a new kind of hunter compared to what already existed? Otherwise the complaint would be, &quot;I could have just bought HH/etc., this was a waste.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..that one on one were often not capable of fulfilling that function. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this contradict your statement that, &quot;Note that I know that HtR games could and certainly did involve sometimes some of the above but the sheer life or death, success or failure necessity of it was removed from the feel of the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is it? Are they removed from the immediate consequences of hunting supernaturals, or are they actually kind of bad at it if they aren't smart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-10-2015, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T07:49:37-08:00","id":365417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365225#post365225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What we're doing is calling him on all the BS he's spewing\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365316#post365316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sorry, you're going to get it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>These sort of lines make your argument come off as belligerent. And at least for me, that makes me hesitant to post in this thread since I don\u2019t come on these forums to be yelled at about how my opinion (and people are just presenting opinions of the materials) is wrong. That being said, my 2 cents follows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365316#post365316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is no logically consistent way to say that a Sorcerer is not a supernatural &quot;creature&quot; but an Imbued is. Either having powers makes you a supernatural, in which case all Numina users are supernaturals, even True Faith ones, or simply having powers is not what makes a character a supernatural critter at which point there's no solid case that the Imbued are anything other than a new type of Numina user with funky rules.<br /> The cWOD has always presented the hunters of the supernatural as people that end up blurring the lines between mortal and supernatural in order to gain the power they need to fight back. HtR is no different in this regard. Drawing an arbitrary line between the Imbued and the hunters presented in other books that use special powers is just that; an arbitrary line. It's only purpose is to try to make a personal preference look like something based in fact instead of just being a personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually an argument to be made for that line. I don\u2019t agree that knowing a couple of spells (hedge magic) or having faith constitutes being supernatural. Hedge magic is represented as something you study at length and can perform. They are rituals that theoretically <i>anyone</i> could do with time and study. Any \u201cnormal\u201d person can learn hedge magic. Faith, for me, only has a system for the player. It specifically says that actual visual in game effects are almost unheard of. It is mainly an internal thing. I do think there is the argument for psychic numina being separate and therefore classifies one as a Supernatural.<br /> But Imbued are different. They undergo a change. One day they\u2019re normal and then *poof* they have powers. For me, that is a supernatural transformation.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365316#post365316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunters don't have a magical power to generate real fire (only does lethal by default instead of Agg, even in crossover)...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that in crossover several of the edges deal Agg. And that the only reason they aren\u2019t listed that way is that the HtR system only deals in normal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T08:48:20-08:00","id":365454,"title":"","content":"To me, it sounds more that Possessed and Moirdryd had a bad play experience with HtR, rather than an issue with how HtR is actually designed to play, or separately what HtR can do. Many of their complaints just don't really jive with the line. Investigation, research, and stakes outs where very much expected from both HH and HtR. HtR being a fully devoted line, didn't make specific rules for it, which maybe they expected, but that doesn't mean it removed that as part of the game either. In fat, most of the fiction, both in the line and in novels, and even in the crossover style books, expressly highlights the fact that HtR cells do a heck of a lot of studying and planning to hunt, and in fact possibly more than HH, for the simple fact that they have more resources (like Hunter.net) to sift through to find the half truths vs the outright BS.<br /> <br /> Unlike with many Numina/True Faith, Edges are neither understood or reliable. They are abilities that the individual Hunters have assigned to them, not that they themselves develop and learn. There are a lot of suggestions on how these can work, but the ability to just spend something from a pool and use a power on command isn't usually one of them.<br /> <br /> While they do have some natural protections against the supernatural (as can HH hunters, sorcerers, etc. . .), something that needs to called out is that they are not 100% protection/immunity, not understood by the individual, and something that, having a very limited resource, especially with new Hunters, needs to be activated, and needs to be activated before hand to have any affect whatsoever, which really plays into the fat that Hunters (HtR) need to pick their fights well, and can not just act any time they see something off. The only universal immunity that doesn't require activation or an experimental effort to function is that they are immune to becoming another supernatural creature, and that's one that is more in place so that a major factor of the setting is not instantly invalidated. (An ex-HtR turned vampire gets on Hunter.net and spills the secrets to the other supernaturals). Hunters can still be charmed, or for a limited time mind-controlled, otherwise corrupted, or manipulated/abused by supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because no two HtR hunters agree on what's really going on, (who/what gave them their abilities, why, etc. . .), and there is no answer given, and the setting itself mandates a contrast between some supernaturals being able to be &quot;redeemed&quot; while it's up to the players to discover and attempt to find out which can not and need destroyed, there is absolutely no built in story, mechanic, or assumption that HtR are just hitmen/women out there to take down monsters with ease. It isn't there.<br /> <br /> Unlike most HH hunters, HtR are random people that have been picked out from the masses, for absolutely no known reason, not given any clue about anything other than monsters exist, and an inborn mandate to do something about it. Some defend against it, some want to heal these monsters, so want to take the fight to them, and some want to try to figure the monsters themselves out.<br /> <br /> So, I don't want to continue the &quot;No, you are wrong&quot; &quot;No you are wrong&quot; sort of deal above, I can see both sides, in my opinion and experience most of the evidence and complaints about HtR above is actually much more true about all of the other HH games, and I'm just not seeing how it was supposed to apply to HtR, but not HH? Kind of seems like a double standard, and I think that's why Possessed is getting so much kickback. Now, that being said, just not digging the game or setting is perfectly fine. And like he or she has said a few times, they are not going to curse WW/OP or you if H20 is a possibility. It sounds more like the argument is focused on how HtR is presented here to others, than actual issues with the game or mechanics, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, being one of the final games to come out, I think HtR did a fantastic job using the ST/&quot;D10&quot; system to allow cool new mechanics and Virtues. I kind if wish some of this could have been ported to the other 20th Anniversary lines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T10:52:01-08:00","id":365528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365417#post365417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These sort of lines make your argument come off as belligerent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say I intended to be belligerent, but I did want my negative emotions about the nature of their posts clear. Seems that came across then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And at least for me, that makes me hesitant to post in this thread since I don\u2019t come on these forums to be yelled at about how my opinion (and people are just presenting opinions of the materials) is wrong. </div> </div> </div>As I said, if it was just, &quot;HtR isn't what I want, so I don't play it,&quot; there wouldn't be heated posting. It's the attitude that they need to come up with all sorts of rationales for it, which tend to lead to saying things that are either nasty by implication (calling Imbued Mary Sues, for example), or inaccurate, which inspires heated defenses against such things<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is actually an argument to be made for that line. </div> </div> </div>Ok. But you never provide a logically consistent definition of that line. Even if the line has theoretic value, if there's no way to actually define it objectively what use is it in application?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t agree that knowing a couple of spells (hedge magic) or having faith constitutes being supernatural. </div> </div> </div>A starting level sorcerer gets 5 dots in their paths. That's a lot more power than &quot;a couple of spells&quot; especially if you're using the Revised rules. True Faith you can make a better argument due to its function. The problem with drawing a line though, is that Imbue Edges are more between hedge magic and True Faith than on the opposite side of the spectrum from them. You can lose your faith and access to those powers, just like you can run out of Conviction and lose access to your powers as an Imbued Neither of these can be regained with some rest and de-stressing. A sorcerer is fairly reliant on Willpower, but that is a self-renewing resource. True Faith and Edges also come from an external source empowered by the users' mental state, while hedge magic is something you study and learn.<br /> <br /> That's my point about logical consistency. Where ever you put the line, you end up with either the Imbue and at least some of the other hunter (not even counting ones like the Children of Osiris) in the supernatural camp, or the Imbued in the mortal camp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Imbued are different. They undergo a change. One day they\u2019re normal and then *poof* they have powers. For me, that is a supernatural transformation. </div> </div> </div>They're externally empowered (hence Imbued), which is why it's sudden. Though there's plenty of evidence in the books that this is really an unlocking of an innate human capability than it is something closer to being Ghouled (ala more akin to how Garou/Fera learn Gifts where a spirit &quot;teaches&quot; them to access something that was always something the Garou had the potential to do rather than actually instructing them in a magical talent).<br /> <br /> However, as you acknowledge already, this puts some Numina users in the supernatural category as well (namely Psychics) since sudden explosions of power are something that can happen to Numina users.<br /> <br /> One day a devout individual can be a normal person, and then the next day a significantly traumatic event can occur that affirms their faith so strongly their devotion transforms into True Faith. They changed. Are they supernaturals and those that developed True Faith more slowly not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was under the impression that in crossover several of the edges deal Agg. And that the only reason they aren\u2019t listed that way is that the HtR system only deals in normal damage. </div> </div> </div>This is addressed in the ST Handbook in its FAQ. The default is that they do not do Agg, even in crossover, though it allows the option of allowing Edges that have flavor text that implies certain weaknesses (usually Fire with Avengers, though the Light powers in Innocence as well) doing Agg, or having that be for special (Merit) Imbued &quot;firebrands.&quot;<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, the one of the reasons listed for why the default is to lethal even in crossover (the fact that HtR just doesn't bother with Agg as a stand alone game is addressed first in the FAQ)? Hunters are human, not supernaturals, thus their powers don't do Agg (which doesn't stop Numina users...). It also goes into this when discussing (on the same page) how the Imbued appear under powers like Auspex 2 (which is that they seem to be human). The FAQ does leave it up to question if the Imbued are humans with powers, or supernaturals in denial about it, but the point of the game is that the Imbued generally do no think they have become inhuman, and that mechanics should not make it obvious, in-character, that this is not the case even if that's how you feel about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T11:23:12-08:00","id":365554,"title":"","content":"It's hard to say as they play at different level IMO<br /> <br /> Hunted is about organisations tht are aware of (some) supernaturals and who work to counter them one way or the other. whereas Reckoning is more about individual who wakes up one days and realizes &quot;What the Hell is THAT thing? And What the Hell is Going on in my Town?&quot; and this revelation fortify him and allow him to acts -along sides other of like mind.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer Hunted, for I prefer the organization level...but it's not to say that those organisation doesn,t have the odd Imbued members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":".  fix typo 01-10-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:31:23-08:00","id":365851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365528#post365528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is addressed in the ST Handbook in its FAQ. The default is that they do not do Agg, even in crossover, though it allows the option of allowing Edges that have flavor text that implies certain weaknesses (usually Fire with Avengers, though the Light powers in Innocence as well) doing Agg, or having that be for special (Merit) Imbued &quot;firebrands.&quot;<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, the one of the reasons listed for why the default is to lethal even in crossover (the fact that HtR just doesn't bother with Agg as a stand alone game is addressed first in the FAQ)? Hunters are human, not supernaturals, thus their powers don't do Agg (which doesn't stop Numina users...). It also goes into this when discussing (on the same page) how the Imbued appear under powers like Auspex 2 (which is that they seem to be human). The FAQ does leave it up to question if the Imbued are humans with powers, or supernaturals in denial about it, but the point of the game is that the Imbued generally do no think they have become inhuman, and that mechanics should not make it obvious, in-character, that this is not the case even if that's how you feel about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Revised and W20 seem to give them much more credit for destructive potential, making the flames produced through Cleave both real and capable of turning a weapon's damage aggravated. Consistently inconsistent across games, is the cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:51:21-08:00","id":366044,"title":"","content":"oh On Werewolf?<br /> <br /> an old crossover idea of mine, is that the &quot;Messengers&quot; are the Weaver, or Servants therof, thoughts on that?<br /> <br /> basicly shes trying to remove anything supernatural from the world., as it interferes with her design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:56:27-08:00","id":366047,"title":"","content":"In Time of Judgment and Apocalypse, one of the possibilities for Reckoning Hunters was that they where actually Imbued to look after the physical world while the Garou fought hell in the spiritual one. Could be a badass crossover event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T02:06:41-08:00","id":366167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365851#post365851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf Revised and W20 seem to give them much more credit for destructive potential, making the flames produced through Cleave both real and capable of turning a weapon's damage aggravated. Consistently inconsistent across games, is the cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't really intended to be crossover rules, they're intended to be quick guides to making NPC supernaturals. Most of those write ups are inaccurate to the rules of the other game lines in general. VtM vampire Disciplines don't work anything like the method presented, and MtA mages don't have paradox that freaking bad. I wouldn't say that WtA Rev. or W20 are solid sources on what the Imbued as supposed to be, but quick hacks of the WtA systems to model the Imbued as in the WtA rules rather than needing to buy up HtR; the write up skips all sorts of Edges, and represents the ones it does with mechanics fairly far away from the HtR ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T03:22:46-08:00","id":366186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=365851#post365851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf Revised and W20 seem to give them much more credit for destructive potential, making the flames produced through Cleave both real and capable of turning a weapon's damage aggravated. Consistently inconsistent across games, is the cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to what Heavy Arms put. Each of the CWoD main lines effectively exist in their own World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T08:56:49-08:00","id":366336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=366186#post366186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To add to what Heavy Arms put. Each of the CWoD main lines effectively exist in their own World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for agreeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T11:20:50-08:00","id":366496,"title":"","content":"To clarify a little on my earlier posting (mostly in response to Heavy Arms)<br /> <br /> Yep. Because it was different. In my opinion it was an un-needed addition to the WoD line when there was an already extant component within the mythos that would have worked really well as a thing instead of a supplementary mention in the form of the Hunters Hunted and other such books. It was a golden opportunity to really outline across the WoD what kind of threat Humanity could be given the chance as was told in most of the Laws of the other game lines. The Numina, the Tools, the ancient knowledge and maybe even artefacts or devices that Hunters used down the years where the natural magic of the World of Darkness bled in and all built off the years of snippets of information and ancillary source books that we'd seen. Something that took things like Hunters hunted, Inquisition, Project Twilight and tidied them up, expanded the ideas and ran as a game. HtR more than anything else felt new for the sake of being utterly new and pretty much ignored the mythos of the WoD, from what I've seen it translates across pretty well into the building blocks that became HtV in the NWoD and it fits well and works there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T11:35:14-08:00","id":366504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=366496#post366496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify a little on my earlier posting (mostly in response to Heavy Arms)<br /> <br /> Yep. Because it was different. In my opinion it was an un-needed addition to the WoD line when there was an already extant component within the mythos that would have worked really well as a thing instead of a supplementary mention in the form of the Hunters Hunted and other such books. It was a golden opportunity to really outline across the WoD what kind of threat Humanity could be given the chance as was told in most of the Laws of the other game lines. The Numina, the Tools, the ancient knowledge and maybe even artefacts or devices that Hunters used down the years where the natural magic of the World of Darkness bled in and all built off the years of snippets of information and ancillary source books that we'd seen. Something that took things like Hunters hunted, Inquisition, Project Twilight and tidied them up, expanded the ideas and ran as a game. HtR more than anything else felt new for the sake of being utterly new and pretty much ignored the mythos of the WoD, from what I've seen it translates across pretty well into the building blocks that became HtV in the NWoD and it fits well and works there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mythos of the classic WoD was being made up as it went. Between that and the Supplement Treadmill that required the regular release of books with little time to spare, I can live with magical They Live. For some of us, it definitely suits the world better than the incongruous atmospheric clash between Mage and everything else.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;the threat of humans&quot;, there were stats for heavy weapons in the 2nd edition Vampire Player's Guide, and Rage Across the Amazon had chemical weapon stats in addition to some of the previous book's heavy weapons and combat vehicles. The threat is the fact that humans make so many tanks that they don't know where to put all of them, and also might engage in frightening NBC warfare at a moment's notice. If a whole bunch of humans don't just look away from an incident, infrastructure goes into action, gets mobilized, and your holdings are going to get blown up or worse. There's the threat of humans, in print since about 1993.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T12:36:22-08:00","id":366544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=366336#post366336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for agreeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, trying to put words in people's mouths around the forums. NOT a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T14:08:34-08:00","id":366615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=366496#post366496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Because it was different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see how we're supposed to read this as anything other than, &quot;I'm not comfortable with saying I don't like the game for no particular reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> Werewolves are different from Gangrel, but since shapeshifters already existed in the WOD werewolves were an unnecessary addition that just does things differently instead of expanding on Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Mages are different from Tremere, but since magic users already existed in the WOD mages were an unnecessary addition that just does things differently instead of expanding on Tremere.<br /> <br /> Mummies are different from vampires, but since immortals that cheated death already existed in the WOD mummies were an unnecessary addition that just does things differently instead of expanding on vampires.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> This logic doesn't work, because it basically turns into, &quot;VtM, by virtue of being first, should be the only cWOD game because it touched on everything in some way first, and expanding those elements in VtM should be done instead of making new games to explore them without being VtM.&quot;<br /> <br /> It being different is a fine reason to say, &quot;Not my bag, so I don't play it.&quot; It being different isn't enough to justify, &quot;it shouldn't have been made.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was a golden opportunity to really outline across the WoD what kind of threat Humanity could be given the chance as was told in most of the Laws of the other game lines. </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of books that do that already. You don't need a core book for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Numina, the Tools, the ancient knowledge and maybe even artefacts or devices that Hunters used down the years where the natural magic of the World of Darkness bled in and all built off the years of snippets of information and ancillary source books that we'd seen. Something that took things like Hunters hunted, Inquisition, Project Twilight and tidied them up, expanded the ideas and ran as a game. </div> </div> </div>What use of that is this to all of us that already have all those books.... because basically cleaning them up and putting them in one place? Sounds like a 20th edition book, not a new gameline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HtR more than anything else felt new for the sake of being utterly new and pretty much ignored the mythos of the WoD, from what I've seen it translates across pretty well into the building blocks that became HtV in the NWoD and it fits well and works there. </div> </div> </div>HtR played plenty of attention to the rest of the cWOD, but like all the other cWOD gamelines it is built somewhat paradoxically to both stand on its own (which the core book(s) focus on) and stand together. HtR has whole books dedicated to relating HtR to the rest of the cWOD mythos. Far more page space in it is dedicated to that than any of the other game lines got.<br /> <br /> And yes, they seemed to have learned their lesson in the nWOD. HtV was probably what HH should have been in the first place, a much more complete book on mortal to minor supernatural hunter organizations with enough meat to be its own game line instead of just being an antagonist book for the rest or only work for very specific modes of play. They seemed to purposefully avoid doing mortal hunters in the nWOD supernatural core books (beyond mortals in the nWOD core book taking on things like ghosts or zombies) and only dealt with dangerous members of their other gameline's mythos. So when HtV came out, it didn't have a HH to compete with and differentiate from.<br /> <br /> But hindsight is a problem like that. I agree the nWOD approach works better, but only because the cWOD approach was messy first.<br /> <br /> And none of this actually makes HtR a bad game; even in the context of the wider cWOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:24:37-08:00","id":367774,"title":"","content":"Personally, I view HtR through the lens of Dark Ages: Inquisition, its counterpart in the Dark Ages line. That is, the Imbued are mortal agents of a higher power that's making a last-ditch effort to save the world. Outside the context of the latter days metaplot, I'm more inclined to say that the Messengers have <i>always</i> Imbued certain mortals to act as their agents on Earth; it's just that without an end-of-the-world crisis at hand, they tended to be more choosy as to <i>who</i> they Imbued, and limited themselves to Imbuing the religiously devout. That is, I treat the mechanics of HtR (with its Conviction, Creeds, Virtues, and Edges) as a reasonable substitute for True Faith: HtR is a game about what happens when the powers normally associated with true faith are instead bestowed on Joe Average. <br /> <br /> I hate the notion of treating the Imbued as replacements for HH-style hunters; I vastly prefer to treat them as complementary things, each with its own focus and role. To the extent that I use HtR material for <i>hunters</i>, I tend to restrict myself to the Bystanders rules, with some slight tweaks (such as renaming Bystander Conviction as &quot;Sanity&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T08:25:35-08:00","id":369760,"title":"","content":"I am very biased here as Hunter: the Reckoning has always been my favorite White Wolf line...but let me tell you my experience with it:<br /> <br /> The first time I read H:tR I was 15-16 years old, and played with some friends that were about the same age. Although we would like to see ourselves as &quot;mature&quot;, we were not, and the core book didn't help: it failed to describe a proper &quot;ecosystem&quot;: on the one hand it was full with illustrations that would make you think you could kill a werewolf with a paperclip and that you could be a BADASS MONSTER EXTERMINATOR that would call hunting &quot;THE GAME&quot; and on the other it told you that you would end up dead if you tried something as innocent as report your zombie neighbor to the police. At that time we obviously disregarded any creed outside Zeal, so we were basically all avengers or defenders: a creed based on trying to &quot;heal&quot; the monsters or wonder whether it's their fault to be monsters? &quot;Yeah, right&quot;. We had a lot of fun with it though, although now I think of the chronicles we would play and can't help smiling. Every time I read people on the Internet bitching about the line, I assume they couldn't get past this first impression of the game, and I really feel sorry for them (not being condescending here, I promise!)<br /> <br /> The second time was 7 months ago. I spent a couple months on a hospital bed and had nothing to read on my computer so I skimmed through 80% of the H:tR line. Now, being 10 years older than I was at that time, I could see a completely different side of the game. Some people in this thread don't like Reckoning because they're essentially &quot;supernaturals&quot;, and that's not only true, but a basic foundation of the line: what would you do if something in your head told you you HAVE to do something with the supernatural? You meet people that hears/sees/feels similar things, although noone knows more than you. The only thing you know is that you'll probably end up dead very soon, but you can't turn your back on this new, terrifying world: the voices won't let you. As you start accepting your &quot;fate&quot; and facing the supernatural, another question arises: how are you not supernatural? You're being told by someone to face something you barely understand, something of which you could be a part of. Also, once you have learned what you can and can't do, and begin to act, you will encounter other hunters that will think that your way is not THE RIGHTEOUS ONE and they might try to frustrate your plans... or maybe even stalk you and kill you if they think you are collaborating with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Note that I am using the words &quot;do something with/face the supernatural&quot; here, as H:tR (for me) is not a game about killing monsters. It is a game about trying to survive from day to day first, trying to understand the monsters second, and trying to make a change in the world third. And the first and second are doomed purposes, as you will inevitably fail to succeed on the first one, either by dying at the hands of a monster or by experiencing the end of the world in first person.<br /> <br /> To me, H:tR is a game about hopelessness. Call me a masochist, but that's what makes it very attractive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3719-cable","user":"Cable","date":". 01-14-2015, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3719-cable","name":"Cable","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3719_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:09:07-08:00","id":377479,"title":"","content":"I think I like the hunters hunted ones, I just like the idea of choosing why you're a hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4786-robinkinser","name":"Robinkinser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:26:51-08:00","id":377504,"title":"","content":"I want to toss my hat in the ring here, and say that I completely agree with Possessed.<br /> <br /> I can not stand Hunter: the Reckoning... for all the same reasons. The entire premise of the game is based on a rather obvious and completely transparent lie, that for some reason no Hunter IC seems to ever figure out.<br /> <br /> I've posted once or twice on these forums with detailed opinions, but after reading through this I feel that Possessed has articulated it well and taken all the heat for me. That being the case, I will just touch on sheer arrogance of the splat:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Reckoning Hunters: Supernatural creatures who murder other supernatural creatures for being supernatural, without ever realizing that THEY are also supernatural murderers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I know they don't all murder... but whatever antagonistic verb you wanna use there applies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hunter: &quot;Yeah so I get these amazing magic powers, but I got to use them to protect humanity.&quot;<br /> Chorister: &quot;Me too!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I should say that I use a more homebrew type of hunter. The only &quot;power&quot; they get is a small piece of the True Faith ability... in that they have a natural resistance to supernatural powers. I tend to think of them as &quot;more human than human&quot;. I also ensure they have no control over this resistance, and that it is something that they were probably born with - but only realized once that &quot;oh shit, Vampires EXIST?!&quot; cherry has been popped.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 01-21-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:17:11-08:00","id":377536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377504#post377504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to toss my hat in the ring here, and say that I completely agree with Possessed.<br /> <br /> I can not stand Hunter: the Reckoning... for all the same reasons. The entire premise of the game is based on a rather obvious and completely transparent lie, that for some reason no Hunter IC seems to ever figure out.<br /> <br /> I've posted once or twice on these forums with detailed opinions, but after reading through this I feel that Possessed has articulated it well and taken all the heat for me. That being the case, I will just touch on sheer arrogance of the splat:</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrogance? Hilarious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reckoning Hunters: Supernatural creatures who murder other supernatural creatures for being supernatural, without ever realizing that THEY are also supernatural murderers.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know they don't all murder... but whatever antagonistic verb you wanna use there applies. </div> </div> </div>Funny, because most monsters tend to be squarely in the camp of 'kill these bastards if they show their faces here&quot;, making every type of monster the top killers of all the other monsters, and with the exception of werewolves, usually of their own. Friendly crossovers are a very rare exception to the rule of &quot;wipe all the others out&quot;.<br /> <br /> And any antagonistic verb? So they all heckle monsters? I suppose some Redeemers fall under that category, depending on how they use the edge that gets monsters to lay their hearts out and tell them about their problems. The intended use of which is to get the monster to stop harming people. Mechanically speaking, Redeemers are probably quite successful in that regard, since they can magically produce fuel stats necessary for some monsters to live via Conviction, but if a monster takes that option, they suffer some really steep penalties from trying to harm humans in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunter: &quot;Yeah so I get these amazing magic powers, but I got to use them to protect humanity.&quot;<br /> Chorister: &quot;Me too!&quot; </div> </div> </div>I honestly can't even parse this as a claim of anything. It's just a couple of sentences that might be related to the topic at hand, with no clearly intended purpose to its comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T15:48:13-08:00","id":377571,"title":"","content":"Saur ops... you dont think its arrogant to lay out a premise that this supernatural creature is the one that represents humanity (though they are super human) while the others are monsters?<br /> <br /> In mage thats called hubris.<br /> <br /> I know you guys really like it and i get that. I have a buddy who only plays reckoning and i dont disparage him for it.<br /> <br /> But the thing is when it came out it felt like a slap in the face. The masquerade, veil, rule of shade all admonish supernaturals to be wary of humanity because it ia dangerous. So they start writing the end of the world and instead of humanity rising up they give us another supernatural splat annointed by God.<br /> <br /> So i guess the masquerade was pointless all along... since humanity stood no chance without being touched by an angel.<br /> <br /> And in regards to the last two lines... if you cant see the similarity between an angel imbued semi-mage and an awakened mage who believes he is a servant of god himself, then i guess it is a worthless statement.<br /> <br /> But listen... lets slow down on the feels here. My opinion is that HtR was a missed opportunity, a bit of false advertising, and an excuse to print a bunch of books. I do not like it at all. You dont agree and thats cool... but to disregard my opinion as illegitimate i think is intellectually dishonest.<br /> <br /> I still like you and want to be your best friend ever. :-P<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: As a stand-alone game, I feel HtR could be fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 01-21-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T16:24:07-08:00","id":377595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377571#post377571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But listen... lets slow down on the feels here. My opinion is that HtR was a missed opportunity, a bit of false advertising, and an excuse to print a bunch of books. I do not like it at all. You dont agree and thats cool... but to disregard my opinion as illegitimate i think is intellectually dishonest.</div> </div> </div> </div>HtR having fans, still, is obvious that despite some people not liking it, is by definition not a missed opportunity. It was a captured one. Because it worked. Whether or not it was chosen over a different viable opportunity isn't the same as it being a missed one.<br /> <br /> The &quot;excuse to print a bunch of books&quot; complaint is meaningless. All RPGs that are sold are an excuse to print books (esp. previous to common place digital distribution). The supplement treadmill was something all of the cWOD lines dealt with. HtR got books because, it being a successfully executed taking of advantage of an opportunity, it sold books. That's what RPG publishers do. They make books for people to buy.<br /> <br /> There's no false advertising that was put out about the game. The game was always very clear about what it was.<br /> <br /> And the issue is not your opinion of disliking the game. It's disparaging the intellectual dishonesty of all the points made against HtR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T16:42:03-08:00","id":377605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377595#post377595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HtR having fans, still, is obvious that despite some people not liking it, is by definition not a missed opportunity. It was a captured one. Because it worked. Whether or not it was chosen over a different viable opportunity isn't the same as it being a missed one.<br /> <br /> The &quot;excuse to print a bunch of books&quot; complaint is meaningless. All RPGs that are sold are an excuse to print books (esp. previous to common place digital distribution). The supplement treadmill was something all of the cWOD lines dealt with. HtR got books because, it being a successfully executed taking of advantage of an opportunity, it sold books. That's what RPG publishers do. They make books for people to buy.<br /> <br /> There's no false advertising that was put out about the game. The game was always very clear about what it was.<br /> <br /> And the issue is not your opinion of disliking the game. It's disparaging the intellectual dishonesty of all the points made against HtR.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was a missed opportunity in my book, because they never talked about the rise of Humanity. They never demonstrated the consequence of failing to maintain the Masquerade. Time of Judgement books tried to touch on this, but so far beyond when it would have been interesting. They could have put HtR out anyway - but they absolutely missed an opportunity.<br /> <br /> HtR and Humanity Rising would not have been mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> You're right about the excuse to print a bunch of books, and I understand that, but it still formed my opinion. I have no need to be convinced, and I realize that all projects are an &quot;excuse&quot; to make a buck... but WHEN it was released, this feeling was relevant. What I wanted would have been a small book, difficult to put on the treadmill. I realize of course that is how business decisions are made... but as I have said multiple times, WHEN it was released it was a slap in the face.<br /> <br /> That's also relevant to my false advertising comment. I don't mean in a legal sense, I mean in a meta-plot sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> I remember someone saying something that fit very well, and will likely never change for me: Which is more normal, Batman or Spiderman? I am firmly and 100% in the Batman camp.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't consider myself a stupid man, but I don't really grasp your last sentence.<br /> <br /> I mean, I am not disparaging anyone's opinion... I am only expressing mine. The question is not one of fact, but rather opinion. People have told me that &quot;are we monsters too&quot; is actually a theme HtR often hits on during actual play, and I appreciate and respect that. Even still... I have no desire to add mage-lite to my game. It does not make logical sense to me, nor does it fit into the WoD cosmology I understand (which includes everything else outside of Exalted or Demon, just because I never got into those).<br /> <br /> I FEEL that Hunter the Reckoning was a missed opportunity (because it would have been cool), a bit of false advertising (because despite what you claim about HtR, the distinct impression myself and everyone I knew at the time had were that we were getting normal hunters, not supernatural hunters), and an excuse to print more books (because delivering an honest mortal hunter book probably couldn't have been spun into an entire game line).<br /> <br /> <br /> Is that better? Is my opinion now acceptable to you? I'm sure I'm still wrong about everything, but I honestly don't give a damn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 01-21-2015, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T16:58:08-08:00","id":377610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377571#post377571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saur ops... you dont think its arrogant to lay out a premise that this supernatural creature is the one that represents humanity (though they are super human) while the others are monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that most of them do anything so grandiose. At least, not without suffering the effects of issues brought upon by Virtues at 7+ dots and/or from their Creed. They just have a new side job scouting out things that ping on their Weird-Shit-O-Meter. They, themselves, don't ping to each other, while every other monster does, so it's actually a somewhat reasonable conclusion to draw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In mage thats called hubris. </div> </div> </div>Mage is a different game. A game where you play someone much more powerful, in a very permissive setting with cosmology that is arguably at odds with every other game. Hence, whatever it's doing, it's free to do by itself. No other game need be concerned with its themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know you guys really like it and i get that. I have a buddy who only plays reckoning and i dont disparage him for it.<br /> <br /> But the thing is when it came out it felt like a slap in the face. The masquerade, veil, rule of shade all admonish supernaturals to be wary of humanity because it ia dangerous. So they start writing the end of the world and instead of humanity rising up they give us another supernatural splat annointed by God. </div> </div> </div>God is absent from this equation. Hell, the Imbued are pretty much an outgrowth of KotE's take on cosmology. Their existence doesn't even really say anything about whether or not humans are &quot;dangerous&quot; on their own, either. Clearly, given the existence of all the ways that they've made to kill each other and the infrastructure or vehicles around them, humans are very dangerous. However, knowledge of the shadows in the corners is a limited, need-to-know kind of thing, and most people ignore it. Imbued are merely put in a place where they have it pointed out to them and cannot ignore it ever again, even if a monster tries to make them ignore it. They otherwise attempt to keep on with lives that don't involve being a psychic FBI agent, hedge sorcerer who researches monsters for a living, or other concepts that involve completely taking someone away from everyday and relatively unspectacular lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So i guess the masquerade was pointless all along... since humanity stood no chance without being touched by an angel.<br /> <br /> And in regards to the last two lines... if you cant see the similarity between an angel imbued semi-mage and an awakened mage who believes he is a servant of god himself, then i guess it is a worthless statement. </div> </div> </div>You're right, I don't see that, because I don't operate off of seeing the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen as angels, nor am I operating from a standpoint where the themes of Hunter are the same as those of Ascension. Imbued are very grounded. Their goal is to stop being victimized, not to snatch a bunch of people up and essentially use them as a machine to rewrite existence. Completely different mood and approach, here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But listen... lets slow down on the feels here. My opinion is that HtR was a missed opportunity, a bit of false advertising, and an excuse to print a bunch of books. I do not like it at all. You dont agree and thats cool... but to disregard my opinion as illegitimate i think is intellectually dishonest.<br /> <br /> I still like you and want to be your best friend ever. :-P </div> </div> </div>I didn't like Hunter when it first came out because humans didn't seem to be underdogs from the point of view of someone so heavily in the camp of &quot;The Red Talons are right.&quot; Now I can appreciate it as a magical They Live, with individuals being squashed underneath a system of oppression they didn't ask for finding that they can kind of see the edges of the system and start pulling at it. Seeing some very faint splashes of Darker Than Black didn't hurt, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T17:09:36-08:00","id":377616,"title":"","content":"@SaurOps<br /> <br /> First of all, I want to thank you for the thoughtful post and responses. I appreciate that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will admit there is a lot I do not know about HtR today. I've read the main book years ago, and I've chatted with friends about it. It sticks in my craw, and I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> At this point my opinion of the line grossly oversimplifies it, I accept that. At the end of the day though... my opinion is that hunters need less supernatural and more wit and grit. That's what I prefer and what I use and it's always been fun to do so.<br /> <br /> Hunter the Reckoning as a stand alone game, I think (as I said before), could be amazing. HtR in a combined WoD I personally feel is incongruent and... just not right. Again... no judgement on you (or anyone) using it, just that I am certain I never will.<br /> <br /> From my understanding the Messengers were Angels. Whatever they were, they had to exist almost outside, or at least above the current WoD cosmology. Maybe this changed or whatever... but it isn't necessary. The role of hunter in my world has been filled... and not by any White Wolf product, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, as a bit of a side note, any crossover game that includes these kinds of hunters (where the PCs are not them) is kind of weird, isn't it? This is a thought experiment for me mostly... but it would seem that the introduction of crazy divine hunters with magic powers sort of misses some of the potential to explore hubris, humanity, etc. If they were more human, they become a sort of reflection of the PCs actions, but when they are so very... inhuman (my opinion) they lose virtually all of that potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T17:59:12-08:00","id":377644,"title":"","content":"I never felt like I would go out of my way to compare H:tR with previous material on mortals confronting the supernatural in the CWoD because the amount of stories, themes and genre's you can play with that basic idea is MASSIVE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:40:34-08:00","id":377728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377605#post377605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HtR and Humanity Rising would not have been mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, of course, the crux of the problem though. &quot;HtR wasn't Humanity Rising, so it sucks,&quot; has zero to do with HtR. It's not a problem with HtR. HtR didn't stop WW from making Humanity Rising (which as you noted, they eventually started on).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WHEN it was released it was a slap in the face. </div> </div> </div>Was Demon getting released a slap in the face?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's also relevant to my false advertising comment. I don't mean in a legal sense, I mean in a meta-plot sense. </div> </div> </div>The Imbued as written were previewed before HtR was published in the metaplot. So no, the &quot;false advertising&quot; thing still doesn't fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember someone saying something that fit very well, and will likely never change for me: Which is more normal, Batman or Spiderman? I am firmly and 100% in the Batman camp. </div> </div> </div>Funny thing.<br /> <br /> Batman is more &quot;normal&quot; but has wildly abnormal problems. Spiderman is superhuman, but has very normal problems. Very few people can really related to being a billionaire orphan olympic athlete genius ninja. Lots of people can relate to trying to balance multiple jobs, conflicting responsibilities, the weight of responsibilities you didn't ask for, etc.<br /> <br /> The &quot;power level&quot; of the characters is not a direct corollary to the kind of stories you tell with them. Batman stories haven't been about gritty street level crime fighting in decades. Batman stories about Bruce Wayne are kind of boring and make him a huge asshole you'd never want to hang out with. Spiderman consistently has stories that make Peter Parker a pretty interesting guy powers or not.<br /> <br /> Batman is more normal in plenty of definitions of the term. But Spiderman's stories are more normal.<br /> <br /> I actually like the idea of Numina users = Batman, and Imbued = Spiderman as an analogy, because it focuses a lot of what kind of stories the Imbued focus on with an odd balance of human + powers that Batman doesn't really get into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't consider myself a stupid man, but I don't really grasp your last sentence. </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with you not liking HtR. I have a problem with a lot of the reasoning you present because they're either not true or doing the whole, &quot;well it was just my opinion (at the time)&quot; dance to try to avoid being fact checked. It's basically saying that it doesn't matter if it is true or not, your feelings make whatever you say about the game unassailable because they're just opinions. I find that very intellectually dishonest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunter the Reckoning as a stand alone game, I think (as I said before), could be amazing. HtR in a combined WoD I personally feel is incongruent and... just not right. </div> </div> </div>The whole cWOD is inconsistent. Now single combined cWOD can hold all the games together. HtR is actually better fit into the cosmologies of Vampire, Wraith, and Demon (including KotE) than Werewolf, Mage, or Changeling are. It's just not in the core book because it's a bit of a metaplot secret.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my understanding the Messengers were Angels. </div> </div> </div>Sort of.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Messengers are DtF Demons effectively; or at least non-sentient entities the Demons made way back when the war with Heaven was going on to empower and protect humans that followed them against the Heavenly Host. So fallen angels. Or their the product of the fallen celestial beings of the KotE cosmology which is basically the same thing in a different lens. It pretty much means that Lucifer and the Ebon Dragon are the same thing, or avatars of the same thing. The metaplot event that cracked open the Abyssal Prison holding the Demons in the Underworld let said being flip on the human potential for being Imbued which is apparently something they always had but it was shut off (which is an easter egg for Exalted) as part of their End Times ploy as the Messengers started Imbuing again. This very much plays into Lucifer's plans more than trying to get a massive human uprising since individual humans getting powers makes it easier for Demons to manipulate people for Faith; mobs might attack Demons trying to reap Faith.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, as a bit of a side note, any crossover game that includes these kinds of hunters (where the PCs are not them) is kind of weird, isn't it? </div> </div> </div>No more than any of the HH style Numina users. Crazy divine hunters with magic powers was a thing in HH. In fact more so.<br /> <br /> The difference between getting on the downside of the Society of Leopold vs. a cell of Imbued is kind of like the difference between being Batman's enemy or Spiderman's enemy. Batman is going to hit you by being out of the blue crazy prepared with almost magical levels of access to appropriate equipment to deal with your strengths/abuse or weaknesses. Batman knows what you are and is ready for you. The Imbued are like Spiderman. They're going to be going off the cuff the first time. They've got some solid things to rely on, but they're playing on their wits to use a small set of perks against you to maximum effect.<br /> <br /> But both are still, from the perspective of being antagonists in a non-hunter game, crazy divine folks with magic powers (even if one is more subtle about it than the other). Making them work for a game is a matter of tailoring them. Just like tossing vampires into a mage game, or werewolves into a changeling game. How you use them is a far bigger factor in focusing on specific themes than what they are.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Imbued come into a vampire game to stress humanity, you pick non-crazy Innocents and/or Redeemers. Maybe a Judge. Let vampires get smacked with feeling human temporarily again. Force them to face that all the compromises they've had to make as vampires are just that; moral compromises against their human side. Don't toss a squad of Avengers led by a Wayward at them. HtR is more than flexbile enough (and in many ways more flexible than HH or Humanity Rising) for customizing Hunters that can fit any niche you need on a thematic level as small group antagonists. A lot of those powers that get them labelled as supernaturals are exactly what makes them capable of not being weird for this purpose. They have a lot of powers that let them shove the moral and psychological flaws of the major splats in their faces directly. A mob of normal humans are dangerous, but can't force a vampire to consider their humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T19:51:13-08:00","id":377736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377728#post377728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The whole cWOD is inconsistent. Now single combined cWOD can hold all the games together. HtR is actually better fit into the cosmologies of Vampire, Wraith, and Demon (including KotE) than Werewolf, Mage, or Changeling are. It's just not in the core book because it's a bit of a metaplot secret.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find the whole &quot;Fit into KOTE&quot; cosmology about as well as the whole &quot;Everything used to be a fairy until they broke themselves' thing Changelings say. Actually I'd say the whole Demon line is pretty much like that, but that's the game you are playing when Playing Demon. When a Demon shows up elsewhere.. well I'll just point out how very similar changelings and Demons are from a mage perspective and leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T20:47:05-08:00","id":377751,"title":"","content":"Were the Messengers Angels? We were never given a conclusive answer to how they relate to Demon or KotE or anything else outside of Hunter, so there\u2019s no way to know for sure. They certainly were angel-<i>like</i>, though. <br /> <br /> And FWIW: if I\u2019m going to play a HH-style game, I\u2019m probably going to play it more like HtV than like \u201cNumina wielders\u201d. Take Project Twilight as an example: sure, it gave details about psychic phenomena; but I never got the impression that all, or even most, of the government agents the book deals with were psychics. It\u2019s not primarily about humans with powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T21:10:53-08:00","id":377756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377751#post377751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were the Messengers Angels? We were never given a conclusive answer to how they relate to Demon or KotE or anything else outside of Hunter, so there\u2019s no way to know for sure. They certainly were angel-<i>like</i>, though.<br /> <br /> And FWIW: if I\u2019m going to play a HH-style game, I\u2019m probably going to play it more like HtV than like \u201cNumina wielders\u201d. Take Project Twilight as an example: sure, it gave details about psychic phenomena; but I never got the impression that all, or even most, of the government agents the book deals with were psychics. It\u2019s not primarily about humans with powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hermitbook was the source of information on the Burning Woman and Shadow Man figures. I know that people have talked about Demon waffling on the issue, with one presentation of Lucifer claiming that he was behind it and another saying that he has no idea. Ultimately, I don't have the money to pursue the matter further, and don't want to read through D:TF material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T21:12:49-08:00","id":377757,"title":"","content":"If you ever read the set up with Batman(genius IQ, insane amounts of top end training, Olympic athlete,etc) the guy is decidedly NOT what you would call normal. He's an example of an Exalted for a reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The people of Hunter of Reckoning always felt more to me as people were had something channeled through them rather than simply another class of people with paranormal abilities. It's a fine line granted but it felt that way to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:49:37-08:00","id":378197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=377751#post377751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were the Messengers Angels? We were never given a conclusive answer to how they relate to Demon or KotE or anything else outside of Hunter, so there\u2019s no way to know for sure. They certainly were angel-<i>like</i>, though.<br /> <br /> And FWIW: if I\u2019m going to play a HH-style game, I\u2019m probably going to play it more like HtV than like \u201cNumina wielders\u201d. Take Project Twilight as an example: sure, it gave details about psychic phenomena; but I never got the impression that all, or even most, of the government agents the book deals with were psychics. It\u2019s not primarily about humans with powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I were running a HH type game I'd port the shit out of the nonmagical Vigil Groups. I love the Union, it probably is what most Reckoning haters wanted all along. Of course it probably doesn't work with the more simplistic reading of the Masquerade that Cwod uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:55:07-08:00","id":378203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course it probably doesn't work with the more simplistic reading of the Masquerade that Cwod uses. </div> </div> </div>Just interpret it in different way for the sake of your chronicles, and the problem is gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:08:02-08:00","id":378218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/364042-reckoning-vs-hunted?p=378203#post378203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just interpret it in different way for the sake of your chronicles, and the problem is gone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean that's why it might not have worked in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T13:54:39-08:00","id":378349,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve said before that the one part of HtR that I\u2019d use in a cWoD counterpart to HtV would be the Bystander rules found in the Hunter Player\u2019s Guide. I wouldn\u2019t use the rationale given for them; just the bit on what they can do \u2014 which pretty much boils down to things like \u201ccan develop a partial immunity to Masquerade-enforcing powers, such as Delirium or the Mists\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}